# WHAT THIS REPLACES.
#
# The fourth acceptance arm used to be "aarch64 assembly is byte-identical to
# a single-target reference".  That arm is unreachable: it stays red until all
# 127 actionable leaked macros are fixed, so it can never say what fraction of
# the work is done.  Worse, it becomes PRODUCIBLE BUT WRONG the moment the
# register vocabulary alone is fixed -- cc1 would emit a .s file and the arm
# would read PASS while WCHAR_TYPE, DEFAULT_SIGNED_CHAR, BITS_PER_WORD,
# ASM_COMMENT_START and all 91 class-(c) macros still carried the primary's
# values.
#
# This file replaces it with 138 arms, one per macro per base, each of which
# names the macro and prints both values when it fails.  Partial progress is
# bankable: fixing the register vocabulary turns ~23 arms green and leaves the
# rest visibly red, which is the truth.
#
# The measurement itself is scratchpad/macro-probe.sh -- it needs a host
# compiler, binutils and the real build directory, none of which are things a
# DejaGnu board can be assumed to have.  So the harness measures and this file
# scores.  Run:
#
#     scratchpad/macro-probe-run.sh                 # writes /tmp/mtp-out
#     MT_MACRO_PROBE_RESULTS=/tmp/mtp-out/results.txt \
#       make check-gcc RUNTESTFLAGS="multi-target/macro-probe.exp"
#
# IT IS NOT A CEILING.  138 = 127 actionable text-diverging macros + 1 that
# differs in text but not in value (MAX_BITS_PER_WORD, kept as the proof that a
# PASS is reachable) + 10 whose definition text is byte-identical on both bases
# and whose values differ anyway.  About 1049 identical-text non-integer macros
# have never been classified.  Green here means "none of the 138 known ones",
# never "no leak".

load_lib multi-target.exp

if { ![info exists env(MT_MACRO_PROBE_RESULTS)]
     || $env(MT_MACRO_PROBE_RESULTS) eq "" } {
    # Deliberately not a silent skip and deliberately not a PASS.  An arm that
    # reports success when it was never run is the failure mode this whole
    # project keeps hitting.
    untested "multi-target macro probe: MT_MACRO_PROBE_RESULTS unset;\
	      run scratchpad/macro-probe-run.sh first"
    return
}

mt_macro_probe_score $env(MT_MACRO_PROBE_RESULTS)
